    "Notes Updated": "7/30/2024",
    "Scouting Notes": "Power still a WIP, but showing in games more often this year\n Glove at second base is really good, and can handle the other spots in the infield well too\n Still very swing happy, but has great bat to ball skills\n One main concern for me is his load, there's a circular motion with the bat and I think pitchers will take advantage of it the further he moves up the ladder\n He's a good athlete and a good, smart baseball player, still sort of like the Kolten Wong comp I had thrown on him a couple years back",
    "Notes Updated 2": "7/25/2022",
    "Scouting Notes 2": "Filled in at A+ early in 2022 to help with a bunch of injuries. Wasn't a good showing, but looked more comfortable than stats show.\n ACL numbers have been really good.\n Same amount of walks as strikeouts, showing a little pop, though likely will always be carried by hit tool.\n Likely ends up at 2B as a defender, where he should be pretty solid.\n Could be a utility type player. If everything clicks, maybe you get a Kolten Wong?",
